{"ref":"BDB, יָרִיב","hw":"יָרִיב","html":"† I. <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">יָרִיב</span>]</big>  <strong>n.</strong> [<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>opponent, adversary (</strong>Ges<sup>§85 d</sup><strong>)</strong>;—sf. (of Zion), <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרִיבֵךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 49:25\" href=\"/Isaiah.49.25\">Is 49:25</a> (𝔊 <span dir=\"rtl\">רִיבֵךְ</span>, so Du); cf. pl. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרִיבַ֑י</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 35:1\" href=\"/Psalms.35.1\">ψ 35:1</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">לֹחֲמָ֑י</span>); of personal opponent, <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרִיבָ֑י</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 18:19\" href=\"/Jeremiah.18.19\">Je 18:19</a> (𝔊 <span dir=\"rtl\">רִיבִי</span>, so Gie).","next":"BDB, יָרִיב²","prev":"BDB, יָרֵב"}